.TH geectl-push 1  "geectl-push 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-push \- Push the working copy\*(Aqs branch to its origin: the leaf that completes a rebase (`update`, then `resolve`, then `push`). Lease\-guarded: a rebase rewrites commits the remote already has, so the push forces with a lease
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl push\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Push the working copy\*(Aqs branch to its origin: the leaf that completes a rebase (`update`, then `resolve`, then `push`). Lease\-guarded: a rebase rewrites commits the remote already has, so the push forces with a lease
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
